{
  "change": "Evaluated the existing LuaFieldText<32> reader for transient effect-mode and clock labels in actor updates, effect defaults, clock getters, spin advancement and render-time evaluation. Short labels stay on the stack; long labels and numeric coercions retain the existing spill/fallback behavior. No new unsafe code, actor cache, timing algorithm or chart-specific behavior.",
  "retained": false,
  "decision": "Reject this candidate. Allocation traffic decreases, and the clock workload median is faster, but the actor workload is slower in all three adjacent pairs. Fof Guys is also slower in all three pairs; Mawaru is slower in two of three pairs. These results do not justify replacing the current path. Production changes and candidate-only tests were reverted; the report records the rejected experiment.",
